summary:
- topic: Board Member Recognition
  text: The board recognized Jennifer Kinney for her service as her term concluded,
    with members expressing appreciation for her contributions, especially on the
    2040 Comprehensive Plan Committee.
- topic: Student-Led Scholarship Initiative
  text: Student representative Elliot Wertheimer highlighted school activities, and
    fellow student Huck Charv presented his 'Study Abroad Scholarship' initiative,
    having raised $1,200 to help financially disadvantaged students participate in
    foreign exchange programs. Board members praised his initiative and selflessness.
- topic: Staff Recognition
  text: Superintendent Angela Atkinson Duina recognized military, AmeriCorps, and
    Peace Corps veterans on staff, and Assistant Superintendent Johanna Prince, along
    with Kat Cox, celebrated the vital contributions of educational technicians and
    substitute educators.
- topic: Referendum Outcomes & Facilities Planning
  text: The superintendent thanked voters for approving bond referendums for roof
    replacements and secure vestibules at elementary schools. The athletic complex
    referendum failed, prompting a pause for further research and discussion.
- topic: Graduation Venue Discussion
  text: The board discussed potential alternative venues for high school graduation,
    such as the Cross Insurance Arena, due to limitations of the school gym and the
    unreliability of the outdoor field. They decided to survey families and students
    for input on options, considering factors like capacity, cost, and atmosphere.
- topic: Snow Day Policy Update
  text: The superintendent announced that remote learning days would no longer be
    used for snow days, citing educational reasons, especially for younger learners.
    Instead, the first two snow days are built into the calendar, and subsequent days
    (up to five) will be added to the end of the school year. Teachers' union representatives
    expressed concerns about the lack of clarity and impact on staff plans, advocating
    for collaboration on a revised plan.
- topic: Service Employees Contract Ratification
  text: The board ratified the FY2024-27 contract for the SouthPortlandSchool District
    ServiceEmployeesAssociation. Board members involved in negotiations commended
    the collaborative and professional process, acknowledging the strong advocacy
    for employees' interests.
- topic: Community Mental Health Support
  text: A citizen speaker thanked the district for its ongoing focus on mental health,
    highlighting improved communication and resources for families, including the
    988 crisis number on student IDs and curriculum support at the middle school.
